<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh's forex market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh's forex market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh's foreign exchange market was closed on Monday because of a two-day public holiday marking the silver jubilee celebration of the country's independence.</p>
<p>The taka was quoted at 42.5470/5480 against the dollar on the last interbank trading on Saturday. Friday is the weekend in Moslem Bangladesh.</p>
<p>The market will reopen on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
</text>
